Dear Moisés,

Yes you have to multiply by the exponential of the offset in order to have it in the outcome's scale. The big differences in model fitted values and observations you had is due to the fact that RMSE and MAE are absolute scale measures that make more sense in models with identity link. For log link a relative measure (scaled?) will make more sense.

best regards,
Elias

