Dear all,

I am trying to implement a non-stationary model which considers elevation at the mesh vertices.  I have a elevation grid for my entire region of interest and I would like to compute

(A^T*elev) /A^T, so that I have the right weights at the mesh vertices.

I set up my A matrix as
A<-inla.spde.make.A(mesh, loc=coords.stations)

but I cannot extract the mesh coordinates from my elev data, because with left_join I need to reduce the decimals of my long,lat coordinate pair, as this only works for 2-3 decimal places.

Do you have any idea how I can get to (A^T*elev) /A^T?

Appreciate your answer.
Corinna

From uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com  Wed Apr 19 10:52:36 2023
From: uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com (Finn Lindgren)
Date: Wed, 19 Apr 2023 10:52:36 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] elevation at mesh vertices
Message-ID: <OGukkmuMbSE.Zd6d0ftWAQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <OGukkmuMbSE.HxrgWr5VAQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <OGukkmuMbSE.HxrgWr5VAQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/OGukkmuMbSE/m/Zd6d0ftWAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

To aggregate gridded elevation onto the mesh I would suggest doing

A <- inla.spde.make.A(mesh, loc = grid_locations)
values_on_mesh <- (t(A) %*% grid_values) / colSums(A)

This takes the weighted averages of elevation, with weights equal to
the "hat" basis functions on the mesh.
(Your alternative formula with "/ A^T" isn't well defined since A is a
matrix, and you need to use the A matrix for the gridded locations.)

Finn

